# 360walkaround/.gitattributes — CONTRACT §1.4.
#
# ⛔ These two files' sha256 is a CONTRACT FACT: the frozen set's harness prints its hash first and
# REFUSES on a wrong count or split, and the WHAT-check prompt is versioned by content. This machine's
# `core.autocrlf=true` would rewrite every LF to CRLF on checkout and silently change both hashes —
# which is a contract fact quietly becoming false, not a formatting preference.
#
# T06 creates the two files; the pin is here from T01 so it can never arrive after the first checkout.
server/prompts/frozen-set-360.json text eol=lf
server/prompts/what-check.md text eol=lf

# ── V2 (board 360-v2) — the same law, now over the pipeline's recorded hashes (T08, F-360-132) ──
# MEASURED, not assumed: `git cat-file --filters HEAD:tours/pilot-karnei/plan.json` on this machine
# (`core.autocrlf=true`, `text` unspecified) writes **1743 CRLF pairs, sha256 6ecd11ef…**, while all
# twelve of `manifest.json`'s render rows record the LF hash **d39ae01d…**. So on a FRESH CLONE:
#   · `render_tour.mjs`'s rerun-skip keys on that hash ⇒ it re-renders all 12 points (~1908 s of GPU)
#     for a line-ending reason;
#   · `assemble_tour.mjs` refuses every scene as a STALE render (loudly, and wrongly);
#   · `assemble_tour.mjs`'s own bytes feed `tour.json`'s `meta.assembled.tool_sha256`, and `plan.json`
#     / `manifest.json` feed `meta.plan.sha256` / `meta.manifest.sha256` — so the committed `tour.json`
#     stops being what the assembler produces, and T08's byte-identical-rerun criterion is false.
# ⇒ every file whose sha256 is RECORDED somewhere downstream is pinned to LF. ⛔ Add a line here the
#   moment a new file's hash becomes a checkpoint; a hash of a file git is allowed to rewrite is not a
#   checkpoint.
tours/*/plan.json text eol=lf
tours/*/manifest.json text eol=lf
tours/*/tour.json text eol=lf
pipeline/assemble_tour.mjs text eol=lf

